.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-ZFS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-zfs
.Nd snapshot, replicate and roll back ZFS datasets from a few dialog boxes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A small graphical front end, for the desktop, over the ZFS commands
people are wary of.
It offers: snapshot a dataset; replicate a snapshot to another pool;
roll a dataset back to a snapshot; show the pools' status.
It runs as the desktop user and asks for the administrator's password
through polkit for the steps that change anything.
It needs a desktop session.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /tmp/kldzfs.err
The last replication's errors.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-rollback 8 ,
.Xr ksnap 8 ,
.Xr zfs-rollback 8 ,
.Xr zfs-send 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Replicate offers the same three destinations on every machine: pools
named
.Ql tank
and
.Ql rpool
here, and a host named
.Ql fiend ,
reached as
.Ql admin
over ssh \(em the author's own lab.
The send to that host runs as the desktop user, without polkit, and
none of the sends is raw, so an encrypted dataset does not replicate.
.Pp
Roll back destroys every snapshot newer than the one chosen
.Pq Ql zfs rollback -r ;
its question warns about losing changes, not about those snapshots.
